486
00:26:17,261 --> 00:26:19,660
Since then, he's come up with his own unique recipe

487
00:26:19,661 --> 00:26:21,860
for micro-brewed root beer.

488
00:26:21,861 --> 00:26:24,580
We're somewhere halfway between those really hardcore root

489
00:26:24,581 --> 00:26:26,980
beers than a commercial root beer.

490
00:26:26,981 --> 00:26:28,880
We're using nutmeg.

491
00:26:28,881 --> 00:26:31,580
And this is the whole nutmeg.

492
00:26:31,581 --> 00:26:33,520
Generally, it's ground.

493
00:26:33,521 --> 00:26:37,120
Then we use cloves, the star anise.

494
00:26:37,121 --> 00:26:39,500
That comes from Spain.

495
00:26:39,501 --> 00:26:41,200
We use the cinnamon sticks.

496
00:26:41,201 --> 00:26:44,220
Cinnamon comes originally from Salon.

497
00:26:44,221 --> 00:26:45,760
We also use the vanilla beans.

498
00:26:45,761 --> 00:26:49,140
We like to use the Madagascar vanilla beans.

499
00:26:49,141 --> 00:26:51,400
Licorice comes from France.

