00:27:38,981 --> 00:27:40,480
Do you serve them over ice?

519
00:27:40,481 --> 00:27:41,480
Absolutely not.

520
00:27:44,520 --> 00:27:46,500
They were built perfectly the way they were,

521
00:27:46,501 --> 00:27:48,700
not to be diluted with ice.

522
00:27:48,701 --> 00:27:51,000
So for us, when we serve up these sodas,

523
00:27:51,001 --> 00:27:52,440
we do it with attitude.

524
00:27:52,441 --> 00:27:56,040
For one major soft drink outlet,

525
00:27:56,140 --> 00:28:00,680
it's not attitude that seems to matter, but size.

526
00:28:00,780 --> 00:28:03,180
Grab a straw and loosen your belt.

527
00:28:09,700 --> 00:28:15,100
The seventh month of the year, the 11th day of the month.

528
00:28:15,200 --> 00:28:18,800
What better date for 7-Eleven to celebrate its birthday?

529
00:28:22,440 --> 00:28:25,440
By offering the public free of charge

530
00:28:25,540 --> 00:28:29,240
its signature soft drink, the Slurpee.

531
00:28:29,340 --> 00:28:32,180
This happens every year on 7-Eleven's birthday.

532
00:28:32,280 --> 00:28:36,680
We give free Slurpee to everybody all day long.

533
00:28:36,780 --> 00:28:39,200
The semi-frozen mixture of water,

534
00:28:39,300 --> 00:28:43,500
flavored syrup, and CO2 has filled more than 6 billion

535
00:28:43,600 --> 00:28:48,100
Slurpee cups since it hit 7-Eleven stores in 1965.

536
00:28:48,200 --> 00:28:51,500
That's enough Slurpee for nearly every person on the planet.

537
00:28:51,501 --> 00:28:53,300
Yeah, actually, this is my first Slurpee.

538
00:28:53,400 --> 00:28:55,400
We don't actually sell Slurpees or anything in England.

539
00:28:59,840 --> 00:29:03,040
Really good, really refreshing.

540
00:29:03,140 --> 00:29:07,340
The Slurpee is in a soft drink category all its own.

541
00:29:07,440 --> 00:29:11,360
It all started in 1959, kind of by accident.

542
00:29:11,460 --> 00:29:14,860
Slurpee began with a broken soda dispenser.

543
00:29:14,960 --> 00:29:18,560
The gentleman who owned the store couldn't serve any sodas,

544
00:29:18,660 --> 00:29:20,960
couldn't serve them warm, so they threw them in the freezer

545
00:29:20,961 --> 00:29:24,000
freezer, and when he served them, all of his customers

546
00:29:24,100 --> 00:29:27,840
love this kind of half-frozen, icy treats.

547
00:29:27,940 --> 00:29:30,800
Six years later, 7-Eleven began selling a modified

548
00:29:30,900 --> 00:29:34,800
version of the beverage it originally called the icy.

549
00:29:34,900 --> 00:29:37,880
After a few years, in 1967, they're sitting around

550
00:29:37,980 --> 00:29:40,420
drinking the drinks and notice that it made this slurping

551
00:29:40,520 --> 00:29:42,620
sound.

552
00:29:42,720 --> 00:29:44,420
So there came the name Slurpee.

553
00:29:46,920 --> 00:29:49,760
The frozen flavors started with Coke, lemon, lime,

554
00:29:49,761 --> 00:29:51,960
and cherry.

555
00:29:52,060 --> 00:29:54,700
Today, 20 different flavors are available,

556
00:29:54,800 --> 00:29:57,400
including energy Slurpees and sugar-free.

557
00:30:02,200 --> 00:30:05,500
Sometimes we get customers who wear the mix and match flavors

558
00:30:05,600 --> 00:30:08,720
to give them the special taste.

559
00:30:08,820 --> 00:30:11,180
The core of every Slurpee's taste

560
00:30:11,280 --> 00:30:16,420
is in the flavored syrup held in 2 and 1 half gallon boxes.

561
00:30:16,520 --> 00:30:19,220
The 2 and 1 half gallon bag in the box

562
00:30:19,221 --> 00:30:24,820
will make a little over 150 22-ounce Slurpee drinks.

563
00:30:24,920 --> 00:30:27,420
The Slurpee syrup is a special formulation,

564
00:30:27,520 --> 00:30:31,260
different than fountain syrup, in that it has an ingredient

565
00:30:31,360 --> 00:30:33,840
which allows the CO2 carbon dioxide

566
00:30:33,940 --> 00:30:36,440
to actually be absorbed into the drink.

567
00:30:36,540 --> 00:30:39,580
That's why Slurpee has that very smooth texture.

568
00:30:39,680 --> 00:30:43,880
The foaming agent is called yucca.

569
00:30:43,980 --> 00:30:46,920
A compressor pumps the syrup, water, and CO2

570
00:30:46,921 --> 00:30:49,960
out to the dispenser, where sub-freezing temperatures

571
00:30:50,060 --> 00:30:53,560
give the Slurpee its trademark consistency.

572
00:30:53,660 --> 00:30:56,660
The sweetener in the syrup allows the product

573
00:30:56,760 --> 00:31:01,360
to be poured at a temperature of 24 to 28 degrees

574
00:31:01,460 --> 00:31:03,400
in a semi-frozen state.

575
00:31:03,500 --> 00:31:07,980
Without that, it would freeze rock solid.

576
00:31:08,080 --> 00:31:11,780
Inside the Slurpee dispenser, water, syrup, and CO2

577
00:31:11,880 --> 00:31:16,920
mix together, then go into each of the machines.

578
00:31:16,921 --> 00:31:19,720
chilled aluminum barrels.

579
00:31:19,820 --> 00:31:25,720
Each barrel holds 176 ounces of finished product.

580
00:31:25,820 --> 00:31:31,960
The brains of the equipment are behind these panels, which

581
00:31:32,060 --> 00:31:35,680
are constantly monitoring what's going on with the product

582
00:31:35,780 --> 00:31:38,880
and the barrel.

583
00:31:38,980 --> 00:31:40,680
A computer monitors the resistance

584
00:31:40,780 --> 00:31:43,220
of each barrel's mixing bar.

585
00:31:43,221 --> 00:31:46,920
As the Slurpee freezes, resistance increases.

586
00:31:47,020 --> 00:31:49,360
When it gets to that ideal point,

587
00:31:49,460 --> 00:31:51,360
the compressor will turn off.

588
00:31:51,460 --> 00:31:55,500
The product then will start to melt down ever so slightly.

589
00:31:55,600 --> 00:31:58,440
The whole key is that when that customer walks up

590
00:31:58,540 --> 00:32:06,580
to the machine, that product in the barrel

591
00:32:06,680 --> 00:32:10,940
is ready to pour that perfect Slurpee.

592
00:32:11,040 --> 00:32:13,220
Slurpees, of course, aren't the only soft drink

593
00:32:13,221 --> 00:32:19,460
at 7-Eleven, a variety of sodas are available by the Gulf.

594
00:32:19,560 --> 00:32:24,600
In 1973, 7-Eleven launched its first Gulf fountain program

595
00:32:24,700 --> 00:32:29,800
with two sizes, which was a 12 and a 20 ounce size Gulf.

596
00:32:29,900 --> 00:32:34,900
In 1976, 7-Eleven launched a 32 ounce big Gulf

597
00:32:35,000 --> 00:32:37,740
and had tremendous success and found that its fountain

598
00:32:37,840 --> 00:32:41,040
business nearly doubled.

599
00:32:41,140 --> 00:32:43,220
Over the years, 7-Eleven has also

600
00:32:43,221 --> 00:32:45,860
a parade of eye-popping serving sizes

601
00:32:45,960 --> 00:32:48,220
that redefined our sense of indulgence.

602
00:32:52,060 --> 00:32:56,060
In 1984, the 44-ounce Super Big Gulp

603
00:32:56,160 --> 00:32:59,980
came in a tapered version for the traveling soda drinker.

604
00:33:00,080 --> 00:33:03,780
1988 introduced the 64-ounce Double Gulp,

605
00:33:03,880 --> 00:33:06,780
which had twice the calories of the original gulp.

606
00:33:06,880 --> 00:33:10,280
I do drink Coke 64 ounces once a day.

607
00:33:10,380 --> 00:33:11,680
Kind of the piece de resistance,

608
00:33:11,681 --> 00:33:17,380
the official team gulp, which is about 128 ounces.

609
00:33:17,480 --> 00:33:20,480
Whatever size is your fancy, 7-Eleven

610
00:33:20,580 --> 00:33:23,120
made filling up on soft drinks a lot easier

611
00:33:23,220 --> 00:33:27,360
by introducing its self-serve fountains in 1978.

612
00:33:27,460 --> 00:33:30,760
But today, soda fans can still be served classic soft drinks

613
00:33:30,860 --> 00:33:35,600
mixed the old-fashioned way at places like the Fair Oaks

614
00:33:35,700 --> 00:33:39,300
Pharmacy and Soda Fountain in South Pasadena, California.

615
00:33:39,301 --> 00:33:42,600
Soda fountains probably hit prominence in the late 1800s

616
00:33:42,700 --> 00:33:46,540
and moved into the early 1900s, whereas soda jerks like myself

617
00:33:46,640 --> 00:33:49,840
would jerk on this handle where the name soda jerk comes from,

618
00:33:49,940 --> 00:33:53,540
and carbonated water would dispense out.

619
00:33:53,640 --> 00:33:56,360
To speed up service, the Fair Oak soda fountain

620
00:33:56,460 --> 00:33:59,260
disconnected its vintage handles a few years back,

621
00:33:59,360 --> 00:34:01,060
and workers now take a modern approach

622
00:34:01,160 --> 00:34:03,960
when adding their carbonated water.

623
00:34:04,060 --> 00:34:06,260
What's really significant about soda fountains

624
00:34:06,261 --> 00:34:09,060
is that you can add different flavors,

625
00:34:09,160 --> 00:34:11,460
like cherry or vanilla, which were really popular

626
00:34:11,560 --> 00:34:14,760
in the old days, and they're still popular now.

627
00:34:14,860 --> 00:34:16,500
Another popular choice served here

628
00:34:16,600 --> 00:34:20,700
is one only your grandfather might remember, the ricky.

629
00:34:20,800 --> 00:34:22,700
This was originally an alcoholic beverage,

630
00:34:22,800 --> 00:34:25,620
but the soda fountain kind of adopted to its own.

631
00:34:25,720 --> 00:34:30,420
So simple ingredients, mix them together,

632
00:34:30,520 --> 00:34:31,920
and this makes a lime ricky.

633
00:34:31,921 --> 00:34:36,660
There's also the phosphate.

634
00:34:36,760 --> 00:34:39,160
It contains an ingredient that works wonders

635
00:34:39,260 --> 00:34:41,860
as a rust remover.

636
00:34:41,960 --> 00:34:45,140
The phosphate is basically a lime ricky

637
00:34:45,240 --> 00:34:47,600
with the addition of phosphoric acid,

638
00:34:47,700 --> 00:34:52,040
which gives it a sour kick, makes it a sour soda.

639
00:34:52,140 --> 00:34:55,180
And there's a lime phosphate.

640
00:34:55,280 --> 00:34:57,280
And then there's a New York favorite,

641
00:34:57,380 --> 00:35:01,920
the egg cream, which contains neither egg nor cream.

642
00:35:01,921 --> 00:35:06,220
It's basically milk, carbonated water,

643
00:35:06,620 --> 00:35:08,860
and then add some chocolate sauce.

644
00:35:10,100 --> 00:35:13,420
It's a really pretty drink because the foam stays wide on top

645
00:35:13,421 --> 00:35:15,540
while the rest of the drink gains the chocolate color.

646
00:35:16,100 --> 00:35:19,980
And you just mix it up like that, and you have an egg cream.

647
00:35:22,080 --> 00:35:24,580
And if you want a glass of plain old soda water,

648
00:35:25,180 --> 00:35:26,340
there's the two-cent plain.

649
00:35:26,700 --> 00:35:29,560
It's not two cents anymore, but it's still a two-cent plain.

650
00:35:31,920 --> 00:35:35,720
The only thing better than a visit to a vintage soda fountain

651
00:35:35,721 --> 00:35:39,220
is the convenience of a fountain in your own home.

652
00:35:39,221 --> 00:35:41,920
And more and more soft drink lovers like Randy Olson

653
00:35:41,921 --> 00:35:45,460
are giving in to the temptation.

654
00:35:45,461 --> 00:35:46,800
You guys want straws?

655
00:35:46,801 --> 00:35:48,940
I put it in because I thought it was cool.

656
00:35:48,941 --> 00:35:50,780
I mean, I thought it was a really great thing

657
00:35:50,781 --> 00:35:52,700
to have a soda dispenser in my theater.

658
00:35:52,701 --> 00:35:54,980
When people come over, they walk into the theater,

659
00:35:54,981 --> 00:35:56,780
and the first thing they do is they look into the room,

660
00:35:56,781 --> 00:36:01,920
and they see the soda dispenser and go, why?

661
00:36:01,921 --> 00:36:04,740
Well, when you sit down and watch a movie, you'll see why.

662
00:36:04,900 --> 00:36:06,300
It's a great thing to have.

663
00:36:08,020 --> 00:36:11,300
The components supplied by Soda Bar System in Wisconsin

664
00:36:11,301 --> 00:36:15,440
are identical to soda fountains at the 7-Eleven or a movie theater,

665
00:36:15,720 --> 00:36:17,520
only on a smaller scale.

666
00:36:18,380 --> 00:36:20,520
All right, one minute to movie time.

667
00:36:20,940 --> 00:36:24,740
Sit in your own movie theater and have fresh soda and popcorn

668
00:36:24,741 --> 00:36:27,260
and hot dogs and enjoy a movie.

669
00:36:27,720 --> 00:36:29,020
How does it get any better than that?

670
00:36:29,021 --> 00:36:32,620
You think soft drinks in a movie are a blast?

671
00:36:32,720 --> 00:36:35,720
This little piece of candy takes the term soda fountain

672
00:36:35,820 --> 00:36:37,220
to a whole new level.

673
00:36:41,360 --> 00:36:45,740
In a soft drink world dominated by Coke and Pepsi

674
00:36:45,840 --> 00:36:50,180
that seemingly caters only to mainstream tastes,

675
00:36:50,280 --> 00:36:52,180
there's still room for a maverick.

676
00:36:52,181 --> 00:36:55,980
a maverick.

677
00:36:56,080 --> 00:37:00,580
Since 1987, Seattle-based Jones Soda

678
00:37:00,680 --> 00:37:03,820
has carved a small but significant niche in the industry

679
00:37:03,920 --> 00:37:06,420
with an unconventional approach.

680
00:37:06,520 --> 00:37:08,660
There's so many different choices out there.

681
00:37:08,760 --> 00:37:11,160
We had to find a way to really, really connect with everyone

682
00:37:11,260 --> 00:37:13,760
in a unique way.

683
00:37:13,860 --> 00:37:16,940
Jones Soda makes a cola and root beer,

684
00:37:17,040 --> 00:37:20,340
but it's the eye-catching flavors like berry lemonade,

685
00:37:20,341 --> 00:37:25,340
strawberry lime, and blue bubblegum that draw curiosity.

686
00:37:25,440 --> 00:37:27,440
The blue bubblegum is pretty tasty.

687
00:37:27,540 --> 00:37:29,280
I like that.

688
00:37:29,380 --> 00:37:31,380
But Jones really pushes the envelope

689
00:37:31,480 --> 00:37:35,780
in its holiday specialty packs flavors.

690
00:37:35,880 --> 00:37:37,700
I'm trying Christmas tree.

691
00:37:37,800 --> 00:37:41,700
Smelling like the woods here, but here we go.

692
00:37:41,800 --> 00:37:44,200
It's not bad.

693
00:37:44,300 --> 00:37:45,300
Sweet potato soda.

694
00:37:45,301 --> 00:37:51,300
I don't think these are going to surpass colas anytime soon.

695
00:37:51,400 --> 00:37:55,040
This is a Christmas ham I'm going to try.

696
00:37:55,140 --> 00:37:57,940
How do you make a soda taste like a ham?

697
00:37:58,040 --> 00:38:01,080
To solve that riddle, Jones turned to its business allies,

698
00:38:01,180 --> 00:38:04,020
the flavor chemists at Virginia Dare Extract Company

699
00:38:04,120 --> 00:38:04,960
in Brooklyn.

700
00:38:05,060 --> 00:38:07,060
When I saw it on paper, I kind of laughed.

701
00:38:07,160 --> 00:38:09,160
It was surprising that somebody would want to drink something

702
00:38:09,260 --> 00:38:10,900
like this.

703
00:38:11,000 --> 00:38:12,820
Using various chemical compounds

704
00:38:12,821 --> 00:38:15,060
compounds in years of experience,

705
00:38:15,061 --> 00:38:17,060
the chemists assemble a flavor formula

706
00:38:17,061 --> 00:38:19,460
to emulate each food's taste characteristics.

707
00:38:24,100 --> 00:38:26,660
A simple taste test helps ensure the formula's taste

708
00:38:26,661 --> 00:38:29,580
is as close as possible to that of the target food.

709
00:38:34,100 --> 00:38:38,580
The smoke is just right past the meaty notes.

710
00:38:38,581 --> 00:38:39,820
So we did a good job.

711
00:38:39,821 --> 00:38:40,820
We did a good job.

712
00:38:40,821 --> 00:38:41,820
OK.

713
00:38:41,821 --> 00:38:46,820
Oh, no way.

714
00:38:46,821 --> 00:38:50,820
I definitely got the aftertaste of the ham.

715
00:38:50,821 --> 00:38:52,820
No need for Thanksgiving or Christmas this year.

716
00:38:52,821 --> 00:38:54,820
You smell really bad now.

717
00:38:54,821 --> 00:38:57,820
In addition to its distinctive flavors,

718
00:38:57,821 --> 00:39:00,820
another concept individual to Jones

719
00:39:00,821 --> 00:39:02,820
is the way it labels its bottles.

720
00:39:02,821 --> 00:39:05,820
People can send in a photograph of their favorite moment,

721
00:39:05,821 --> 00:39:08,820
and anybody has a chance to get on to a soda bottle.

722
00:39:08,821 --> 00:39:11,120
anybody has a chance to get onto a soda bottle.

723
00:39:11,560 --> 00:39:13,440
You know, only Michael Jordan can get on Wheaties,

724
00:39:13,580 --> 00:39:15,420
but anybody can get on a bottle at Jones.

725
00:39:16,140 --> 00:39:19,420
And if you want to guarantee your picture will make it onto a bottle...

726
00:39:20,200 --> 00:39:23,620
My Jones is a very unique process for Jones soda.

727
00:39:24,020 --> 00:39:25,780
Upload a photo to the website,

728
00:39:26,040 --> 00:39:28,740
and we'll send 12 bottles to their door,

729
00:39:29,120 --> 00:39:32,020
whatever flavor they want, with their picture on it.

730
00:39:33,520 --> 00:39:36,160
In recent years, Jones soda wedged its way

731
00:39:36,161 --> 00:39:39,160
two soft drink markets once reserved only for the Cola

732
00:39:39,260 --> 00:39:41,460
Giants.

733
00:39:41,560 --> 00:39:44,960
The first, commercial airline beverage service,

734
00:39:45,060 --> 00:39:49,300
with its partner, Alaska Airlines.

735
00:39:49,400 --> 00:39:53,420
The second, the Seattle Seahawks concession stand.

736
00:39:53,520 --> 00:39:56,520
Out of all the NFL football teams in the country,

737
00:39:56,620 --> 00:40:00,920
I think 14 serve Pepsi, 16 serve Coke,

738
00:40:01,020 --> 00:40:03,320
and one serves Jones.

739
00:40:03,420 --> 00:40:05,160
To produce a specialty pack of sodas

740
00:40:05,161 --> 00:40:08,600
tailor-made for football fans.

741
00:40:08,700 --> 00:40:10,560
Jones once again tapped the expertise

742
00:40:10,660 --> 00:40:14,200
of the flavor chemists at Virginia Dare.

743
00:40:14,300 --> 00:40:16,500
They've asked us for a grass flavor and a dirt flavor.

744
00:40:16,600 --> 00:40:20,100
And since smell and taste are so closely associated,

745
00:40:20,200 --> 00:40:22,120
everybody knows what grass and dirt smells like.

746
00:40:22,220 --> 00:40:26,720
So I tried to formulate flavors that smelled like these items

747
00:40:26,820 --> 00:40:29,420
rather than actually tasted like them.

748
00:40:29,520 --> 00:40:31,960
Perspiration, it's quite unusual if you want to drink it.

749
00:40:32,060 --> 00:40:34,220
But there's a distinct odor to perspiration.

750
00:40:34,221 --> 00:40:36,620
and we're able to emulate that with some of the compounds

751
00:40:36,621 --> 00:40:39,160
we have here.

752
00:40:39,161 --> 00:40:40,060
Well, that's nice.

753
00:40:44,960 --> 00:40:48,460
It's actually a little difficult to drink.

754
00:40:48,461 --> 00:40:51,100
When it comes to flavors meant to taste good,

755
00:40:51,101 --> 00:40:54,540
Jones means business, as it produced 6 million cases

756
00:40:54,541 --> 00:40:55,900
in 2007.

757
00:40:55,901 --> 00:40:57,480
We definitely have unique flavors,

758
00:40:57,481 --> 00:41:00,280
but I think any flavor that we put out, even if it is dirt,

759
00:41:00,281 --> 00:41:02,280
it's the best dirt you're going to find in town.

760
00:41:04,220 --> 00:41:06,920
Ah, dirty.

761
00:41:07,020 --> 00:41:09,960
That's not good.

762
00:41:10,060 --> 00:41:12,100
While Joan's soda sometimes pushes

763
00:41:12,200 --> 00:41:16,700
the limits of taste, a performance duo called Epee Bird

764
00:41:16,800 --> 00:41:19,100
has pushed the limits of what a small piece of candy

765
00:41:19,200 --> 00:41:20,700
can ignite in a bottle of soda.

766
00:41:23,840 --> 00:41:27,480
The duo armed themselves with 200 liters of Diet Coke

767
00:41:27,580 --> 00:41:31,880
and 523 Mentos and took an offbeat science experiment,

768
00:41:31,881 --> 00:41:35,820
experiment literally to new heights.

769
00:41:35,920 --> 00:41:40,320
Their artistry became a viral video sensation viewed by millions

770
00:41:40,420 --> 00:41:43,320
on the internet.

771
00:41:43,420 --> 00:41:46,260
Some of the scientific processes underlying the phenomenon

772
00:41:46,360 --> 00:41:48,900
are still a matter of debate.

773
00:41:49,000 --> 00:41:51,660
